1
00:00:02,586 --> 00:00:04,212
Hey, what are you guys
looking at?

2
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:05,422
Oh, it's a poster

3
00:00:05,464 --> 00:00:06,924
for that World War I movie
that I'm in.

4
00:00:06,966 --> 00:00:07,925
Check it out.

5
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:09,134
Yeah?

6
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:10,761
Wow, it looks
really violent.

7
00:00:10,803 --> 00:00:11,762
Uh-huh.

8
00:00:11,804 --> 00:00:12,972
I know.

9
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:14,473
I'm coming soon
to a theater near you.

10
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:15,641
I'm in THX.

11
00:00:15,683 --> 00:00:17,142
I'm unsuitable
for children.

12
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:20,604
Man, I cannot wait
to see this.

13
00:00:20,646 --> 00:00:22,815
Yeah, yeah, it's already
generating Oscar buzz.

14
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:23,858
I started that.

15
00:00:23,899 --> 00:00:24,900
I thought I did.

16
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:26,485
Oh, hey, guess what?

17
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:29,655
I just talked to my agent,
and the premiere is next week

18
00:00:29,697 --> 00:00:31,198
and you're all invited.

19
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:32,783
( gasps )
That's great.

20
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:33,868
Are we going
to take a limo?

21
00:00:33,909 --> 00:00:35,243
Sure, why not?

22
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:37,621
I love taking limos
when nobody died.

23
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:41,458
Well, obviously,
I won't be able to come.

24
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,169
For those of you who haven't
checked their calendars

25
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:45,420
today's my due date.

26
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:47,130
Well, you know

27
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,299
I just want to
take a moment and
thank you guys

28
00:00:49,341 --> 00:00:51,510
for how great you've
been during this time.

29
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:53,428
I really couldn't have
done it without you.

30
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:55,472
And I have loved
these last nine months.

31
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:58,475
And even though I am so
looking forward to the next part

32
00:00:58,517 --> 00:01:01,353
I am really going to miss
being pregnant.

33
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:09,570
That's right,
still no baby.

34
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:11,196
Come on, people

35
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,823
please make some room.

36
00:01:12,865 --> 00:01:15,034
Uh, sweetie, maybe you'd
be more comfortable here.

37
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,452
( deep sigh )

38
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,788
You.

39
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:25,419
Like you haven't done enough.

40
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,922
Look, I know how
miserable you are.

41
00:01:27,963 --> 00:01:30,674
I wish there was
something I could do.

42
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:33,176
I mean, I wish I
were a sea horse.

43
00:01:36,764 --> 00:01:38,306
Because with sea horses

44
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:41,018
it's the male...
they carry the babies.

45
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:47,524
And then also, um, I'd
be far away in the sea.

46
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:01,080
Oh, God.

47
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,372
( moans )

48
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:05,751
I have never been
so uncomfortable

49
00:02:05,793 --> 00:02:07,711
in my entire life.

50
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:08,963
Oh, I know, I've been there.

51
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:10,297
I remember toward the end...

52
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:12,091
Oh, Phoebe,
that's a great story.

53
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:14,426
Could you tell it to me while
you're getting me some iced tea?

54
00:02:16,177 --> 00:02:17,345
( groans )

55
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,680
Oh, God...

56
00:02:18,722 --> 00:02:19,765
Get out!

57
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:22,517
Get out, get out, get out!

58
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:24,895
Let's.

59
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:38,617
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

60
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:40,828
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

61
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,997
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

62
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:47,835
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

63
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:50,129
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

64
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:53,381
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

65
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:56,677
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

66
00:02:56,718 --> 00:03:02,724
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

67
00:03:07,146 --> 00:03:09,064
( groans )

68
00:03:09,106 --> 00:03:11,566
Hey, did you have
the baby yet?

69
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:14,987
Do you want me to come
over there and sit on you?

70
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:16,321
'Cause I'll do it.

71
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:19,407
What are you doing here
so early?

72
00:03:19,449 --> 00:03:20,575
They sent me home
from work.

73
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:21,576
They were, like

74
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:23,411
"Start your maternity leave now.

75
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,288
Just rest.
Get ready for the baby."

76
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:27,082
Well, you know what? Screw 'em.

77
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:30,418
They don't want me there, I'll
just hang out with you guys.

78
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:34,882
Or you could do volunteer work.

79
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:36,675
( phone rings )

80
00:03:36,717 --> 00:03:38,969
Hello?

81
00:03:39,011 --> 00:03:41,180
Joey, it's Estelle. Great news.

82
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:45,433
I was able to get you and one
guest tickets to your premiere.

83
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:47,853
One guest? You told me
I could have six tickets.

84
00:03:47,895 --> 00:03:50,480
Well, I sold four of them
on eBay.

85
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:52,399
( groans )

86
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,402
You'll be sitting
next to HotGuy372.

87
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:57,988
Oh, my God. So that's it?

88
00:03:58,030 --> 00:04:01,075
I only get to bring one guest?

89
00:04:01,116 --> 00:04:03,994
Yeah, what time do you want
to pick me up?

90
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:06,830
Hello?

91
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:08,165
Did you hear that?

92
00:04:08,207 --> 00:04:11,043
I only get one extra ticket
to my premiere.

93
00:04:11,085 --> 00:04:13,879
So somehow I have to pick
between you three and Ross.

94
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:18,842
Wait. Wh-What about me?

95
00:04:18,884 --> 00:04:21,845
Well, you said you
didn't want to go.

96
00:04:21,887 --> 00:04:24,056
I don't, but I would still
like to be acknowledged.

97
00:04:24,098 --> 00:04:26,058
What, just because I'm pregnant,
I'm invisible?

98
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,768
Definitely not invisible.

99
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:33,356
Well, you know, Ross didn't
care enough to be here

100
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:34,816
so I think he's out.

101
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:36,693
You know, you snooze, you lose.

102
00:04:36,735 --> 00:04:39,029
He's not snoozing;
he's teaching a class.

103
00:04:39,071 --> 00:04:40,864
Well, then somebody's snoozing.

104
00:04:40,906 --> 00:04:44,492
And, Joey, not that this
should affect you at all

105
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:46,870
but, um, if you were to pick me

106
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:51,374
I was planning on wearing
a sequin dress cut down to here.

107
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,920
I haven't seen this dress.

108
00:04:54,962 --> 00:04:56,671
Star in a movie.

109
00:04:56,713 --> 00:05:00,383
Joey, you pick whoever
you want, okay?

110
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:02,343
You just listen to your heart.

111
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:03,887
What does it tell you?

112
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:05,597
Phoebe, Phoebe, Phoebe.

113
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:11,352
Well, uh...

114
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:14,022
I think I want to take Chandler.

115
00:05:15,065 --> 00:05:16,817
Phoebe, Phoebe, Phoebe,
Phoebe, Phoebe...

116
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:19,736
( imitating flat-line tone )

117
00:05:19,778 --> 00:05:21,029
You really want to take me?

118
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:22,614
Yeah. Yeah.

119
00:05:22,656 --> 00:05:24,908
I mean, I'm sorry,
I wish I could take everybody

120
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:27,786
but, you know, Chandler's
always supported my career.

121
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:30,664
He's paid for acting classes
and headshots and stuff

122
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:33,458
and, well, this would be my way
of paying you back.

123
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:37,129
So, you're never actually going
to pay me back?

124
00:05:40,132 --> 00:05:42,383
Hey, just because he
paid for your headshots

125
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:43,718
you're going to take him?

126
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,929
Joey, I don't think
you're comprehending

127
00:05:45,971 --> 00:05:48,974
just how slutty
this dress is.

128
00:05:50,309 --> 00:05:52,519
It's not just the stuff
he paid for.

129
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,938
I mean, it's-it's everything,
you know?

130
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:56,773
He... he read lines with me.

131
00:05:56,815 --> 00:05:59,609
He went with me on auditions
when I was really nervous.

132
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:00,986
And then he consoled me

133
00:06:01,028 --> 00:06:03,071
after I didn't get parts
that I really wanted.

134
00:06:03,113 --> 00:06:04,656
You always believed in me, man.

135
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:06,908
Even-even when I didn't believe
in myself.

136
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:08,952
I always knew
you were going to make it.

137
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:10,162
I'm so proud of you.

138
00:06:10,204 --> 00:06:12,622
Thanks. That...

139
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:14,624
that means a lot to me.

140
00:06:17,544 --> 00:06:20,297
Mon, maybe one of these guys
wants to wear your dress.

141
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:22,632
All right,
I'm going to go shave.

142
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:24,259
( clears throat )

143
00:06:24,301 --> 00:06:27,512
Yeah, well,
I'm going to go, uh, spit.

144
00:06:27,554 --> 00:06:29,681
( Rachel groans )

145
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:34,353
Oh, I have to pee.

146
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:35,354
If I don't come out
in five minutes

147
00:06:35,394 --> 00:06:36,688
it's because
I've choked to death

148
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,732
on the potpourri stink.

149
00:06:41,193 --> 00:06:42,610
When she comes out

150
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:44,487
you hold her nose,
I'll blow in her mouth

151
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:46,531
and the kid will just
( pops ) right out of her.

152
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,160
She's over a week late.

153
00:06:50,202 --> 00:06:52,204
She's got to have it
today, right?

154
00:06:52,246 --> 00:06:53,412
I don't know.

155
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:55,707
I think it's still
going to be a while.

156
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:58,126
Mmm. Care to make
it interesting?

157
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:02,130
I bet you that she'll have it
by this time tomorrow.

158
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:03,131
You're on.

159
00:07:03,173 --> 00:07:03,924
Okay, how much?

160
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:06,927
$100,000.

161
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:09,221
How about 50 bucks?

162
00:07:09,263 --> 00:07:11,639
Fine. I'll call Zurich
and move some money around.

163
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:15,810
RACHEL:
All right, whose turn is it
to help me get up?

164
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:18,855
( clears throat )

165
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:20,107
No one's here!

166
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:23,735
Oh, damn it.

167
00:07:28,782 --> 00:07:32,244
( cheering and applause )

168
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:38,666
This is so exiting.

169
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:40,752
So glamorous--
people taking our picture.

170
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:41,920
GIRL:
Joey!

171
00:07:41,962 --> 00:07:43,171
How do I look?

172
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:45,090
A little tall.

173
00:07:45,132 --> 00:07:46,507
What?

174
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:49,052
Do you mind crouching
down a little bit

175
00:07:49,094 --> 00:07:50,387
so I look taller?

176
00:07:50,429 --> 00:07:51,554
( cheering continues )

177
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:52,597
There you go.

178
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,395
It's just so glamorous.

179
00:07:58,437 --> 00:08:00,063
GIRL:
I love you, Joey!

180
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:01,856
( groans )

181
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:04,943
Oh, hey, Mon,
Rach is here.

182
00:08:04,985 --> 00:08:06,569
And you're still pregnant.

183
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:08,405
( Rachel continues groaning )

184
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:09,656
Oh, I'm sorry.

185
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:11,325
I know how uncomfortable
you are.

186
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:13,576
You know what?
You look great.
Oh...

187
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:15,162
Yeah, like 50 bucks.

188
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:20,083
Oh, I have to go pee.

189
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:21,918
Apparently, this baby thinks

190
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:24,087
that my bladder
is a squeeze toy.

191
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:27,924
Oh, damn it. Damn it.

192
00:08:27,966 --> 00:08:29,508
Here's your 50 bucks.

193
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:32,095
That's interesting
that you lost.

194
00:08:32,137 --> 00:08:34,931
Now, I forget,
do you like to lose?

195
00:08:34,973 --> 00:08:36,475
All right, stop it.

196
00:08:36,515 --> 00:08:39,186
Double or nothing
that she has it by tomorrow.

197
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:40,728
Fine. You're on.
Okay.

198
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:43,231
Until then, General Grant

199
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:44,983
why don't you set up camp
right there.

200
00:08:47,027 --> 00:08:48,069
Hey, is Rachel here?

201
00:08:48,111 --> 00:08:49,779
We have a doctor's appointment.

202
00:08:49,821 --> 00:08:51,490
She's in the bathroom.

203
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:53,200
Rach, we got to go.

204
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:54,993
RACHEL:
In a minute!

205
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:59,498
People ask me
why we're not together.

206
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:02,209
I just don't know
what to tell them.

207
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:03,710
RACHEL:
All right,
all right

208
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:05,086
let's go.

209
00:09:05,128 --> 00:09:06,629
ROSS:
Uh, do you want
to go change first?

210
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,465
Doctor's keeping
the office open
late for us

211
00:09:08,507 --> 00:09:09,674
but if you hurry...

212
00:09:11,176 --> 00:09:13,261
No, I'm fine.

213
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:15,680
Really? You don't think
that's a little inappropriate?

214
00:09:15,722 --> 00:09:17,182
What?

215
00:09:17,224 --> 00:09:19,476
Good God, man,
don't anger it.

216
00:09:23,021 --> 00:09:25,232
Ross, it is 100 degrees outside.

217
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:29,152
For the first time in weeks,
I am somewhat comfortable.

218
00:09:29,194 --> 00:09:30,362
Fine, fine,
you know what?

219
00:09:30,404 --> 00:09:31,571
Whatever you want, okay?

220
00:09:31,612 --> 00:09:32,822
You're the mommy.

221
00:09:32,864 --> 00:09:34,657
Uh-uh-uh, pal.
Don't call me mommy.

222
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:37,202
It's bad enough
you call your own mother that.

223
00:09:39,246 --> 00:09:42,123
I'm actually with her
on this one.

224
00:09:47,421 --> 00:09:48,880
JOEY ( in movie ):
I thought I knew

225
00:09:48,922 --> 00:09:50,840
who the enemy was,
but it was you all along.

226
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:52,592
You led them right to us,
didn't you?

227
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:55,554
Okay, this is it-- this is
my big fight scene coming up.

228
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:59,849
...but I'm fighting for every
man in the 82nd Ground Division.

229
00:10:09,443 --> 00:10:10,193
Ross?

230
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:11,611
Yeah?

231
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:13,238
Can I ask
you something?
Uh-huh.

232
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:16,199
When Carol was pregnant
with Ben...

233
00:10:16,241 --> 00:10:17,492
Mm-hmm.

234
00:10:17,534 --> 00:10:19,702
Were you this irritating?

235
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:23,998
Wow.

236
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:24,999
Excuse me?

237
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,251
Uh, nothing, nothing.

238
00:10:26,293 --> 00:10:27,586
You were just, uh...

239
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,963
you've been a little short
with me lately.

240
00:10:30,004 --> 00:10:31,756
I'm not trying to irritate you.

241
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:34,759
Well, then you just must have
a natural talent for it.

242
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:38,054
You know what?
The doctor will be in soon.

243
00:10:38,096 --> 00:10:40,723
Why don't we not speak
until then.

244
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:42,225
Okay.

245
00:10:42,267 --> 00:10:46,438
( sighs )

246
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,607
Seriously, breathe louder, Ross.
That's great.

247
00:10:52,611 --> 00:10:55,696
You know, we should probably
ask the doctor

248
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:58,533
if she even knows how
to deliver a baby

249
00:10:58,575 --> 00:11:01,035
that's half human,
half pure evil.

250
00:11:04,331 --> 00:11:06,374
Hello.
Hi, Dr. Long,
how are you?

251
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:07,584
Oh, you're nice to her.

252
00:11:07,626 --> 00:11:09,127
She has the drugs.

253
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:13,047
We'll do a quick check.

254
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:14,132
Okay.

255
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:16,134
So, eight days late, huh?
Yeah.

256
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:18,011
You must be getting
a little uncomfortable.

257
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:21,473
Yeah, just a tad.

258
00:11:21,515 --> 00:11:24,058
Well, you're about 80% effaced,
so you're on your way.

259
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:26,727
It still could last
